   "evidence": "Line 259 `def electronWeakCharge : \u211d := 2 * C.electron.c1 C.electron` with `variable (C : NeutralCurrentCouplings)` (line 153); `NeutralCurrentCouplings` is the three-field bundle at Parameters.lean:115. Grep for `electronWeakCharge|protonWeakCharge|neutronWeakCharge|nuclearWeakCharge|c1Up|c1Down` across `code/EpsilonEridani` returns only this file, so there are no other call sites to update.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/PVES/Electroweak/LowEnergyCouplings.lean",
   "fix": "Move it into the `FermionNeutralCurrentCouplings` namespace: `def weakCharge (\u2113 : FermionNeutralCurrentCouplings) : \u211d := 2 * \u2113.c1 \u2113`, with `weakCharge_def` and `weakCharge_eq_four_mul_gA_mul_gV : \u2113.weakCharge = 4 * \u2113.gA * \u2113.gV`; restate the tree-level results as `(smTreeLevelCouplings s2).electron.weakCharge = 1 - 4 * s2` and `\u2026 = 0 \u2194 s2 = 1/4`, and drop `NeutralCurrentCouplings.electronWeakCharge` (no compatibility alias).",
   "issue": "`electronWeakCharge` (line 259) and its two general lemmas `electronWeakCharge_def` (271) and `electronWeakCharge_eq_four_mul_gA_mul_gV` (289) take a whole `NeutralCurrentCouplings` but touch only `C.electron`; `C.upType`/`C.downType` are visibly unused. This is the wrong level: the quantity is `2 * \u2113.c1 \u2113` for one coupling pair, exactly like `c1`/`c2`, and the roadmap's M\u00f8ller line (`Examples.Moller`, \"no hadronic input at all\") works at the pair level, where this charge is then unreachable. Contrast `protonWeakCharge`/`neutronWeakCharge`, which genuinely need all three fields.",
   "line": 259
  }
